## ✅ `CustomerEmailTriage.flow` — Complete

**File:** `CustomerEmailTriage/CustomerEmailTriage/CustomerEmailTriage.flow`

### What the flow does

Every email arriving in your Outlook inbox fires the flow. Here's the full path:

```
[Email Received] → [Classify Email] ──success──► [VIP and Urgent?]
                                    └──error───► [Log Error] → [Done — Error]

[VIP and Urgent?] ──true──► [Slack Alert] → [Reply Escalated] → [Done — Escalated]
                  └─false──► [Create Jira Ticket] → [Reply Standard] → [Done — Standard]
```

### The 11 nodes

| Node | Type | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `emailReceived1` | Outlook 365 trigger | Polls your Inbox; fires on every new email |
| `classifyEmail1` | Script | Checks VIP sender (domain/address list) AND urgency keywords — returns `isVip`, `isUrgent` |
| `escalationCheck1` | Decision | `isVip === true && isUrgent === true` → true branch |
| `slackAlert1` | Slack connector | Posts `🚨 VIP ESCALATION — <subject>` to `#SLACK_CHANNEL_PLACEHOLDER` |
| `replyEscalated1` | Outlook 365 connector | Replies to sender: "escalated to our senior team" |
| `endEscalated1` | End | |
| `createJiraTicket1` | Jira connector | Creates issue in `SUPPORT_PROJECT_KEY_PLACEHOLDER` with subject + sender |
| `replyStandard1` | Outlook 365 connector | Replies to sender with their Jira ticket key |
| `endStandard1` | End | |
| `logClassifyError1` | Script | Captures classification errors |
| `endError1` | End | |

### Three things to fill in before deploying

1. **`SLACK_CHANNEL_PLACEHOLDER`** in `slackAlert1.inputs.detail.bodyParameters.channel` → replace with your real Slack channel ID (e.g. `C0123456789`)
2. **`SUPPORT_PROJECT_KEY_PLACEHOLDER`** in `createJiraTicket1.inputs.detail.bodyParameters.fields_sub_project_sub_key` → replace with your Jira project key (e.g. `SUP`)
3. **Issue type ID `10004`** in `createJiraTicket1.inputs.detail.bodyParameters.fields_sub_issuetype_sub_id` → verify this matches your Jira project's "Task" or "Story" type ID (run `uip is resources run list "uipath-atlassian-jira" "issuetype"` against your project to confirm)

The VIP domain/address lists in `classifyEmail1` are also editable directly in Studio Web or the `.flow` file.

